CATEGORIES:ThoughtfulLearning
CATEGORIES:Lecture/Discussion
DESCRIPTION:Full description here: Rebuilding Democracy | Happening @ Mich
 igan\n \nAs the country heads into the 2026 midterm elections\, the Unive
 rsity of Michigan welcomes journalist Osita Nwanevu\, contributing editor 
 at The New Republic and columnist at The Guardian\, for a public conversat
 ion with Elizabeth Anderson\, the John Dewey Distinguished University Prof
 essor of Philosophy.The evening centers on Nwanevu's new book\, The Right 
 of the People: Democracy and the Case for a New American Founding\, which 
 argues that America's democratic troubles run deeper than any single elect
 ion. The real problem\, Nwanevu contends\, lies in institutions that were 
 never designed to let majorities govern\, and in an economy that keeps pow
 er far from ordinary people.Anderson\, one of the country's most influenti
 al political philosophers\, brings her own work on democracy\, equality\, 
 and the workplace to the exchange. Together they take up the questions thi
 s election season keeps surfacing. Who really holds power in America? Why 
 do so many people feel unheard\, and what would it take to build a democra
 cy worthy of the name?The conversation is free and open to students\, facu
 lty\, and the broader Ann Arbor community\, with time for audience questio
 ns.ScheduleFriday\, October 9\, 2026 at Ross School of Business\, Robertso
 n Auditorium5:30 pm Doors open\, light refreshments and Literati book sale
 s in the lobby.6:00 pm The program begins\, including questions and answer
 s at the end.7:30 pm Refreshments and book signing / sales in the lobby un
 til 8:00 pm.\n\nHosted by: Organizer Sixty\n\nAdditional Information can b
 e found at: https://maizepages.umich.edu/event/12720408
DTEND:20261010T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20261009T040316Z
DTSTART:20261009T213000Z
GEO:42.272770;-83.737520
LOCATION:Ross School of Business - Robertson Auditorium
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Rebuilding Democracy Osita Nwanevu in conversation with Elizabeth 
 Anderson on the American Crossroads
UID:https://maizepages.umich.edu/event/12720408
URL:https://maizepages.umich.edu/event/12720408
X-HOSTS:Organizer Sixty
